  "idea": "Raycast vs Alfred: which Mac productivity launcher takes the crown",
  "text": "Why did Raycast's modern UI and free extension store win over power users? Setting up integrations in older launchers meant searching forum threads and configuring fragile, manual scripts. That setup friction forced busy professionals to abandon launcher automations and revert to slow mouse navigation. Raycast fixes this with a verified community store offering instant integrations for GitHub, Linear, and Notion. You trigger cross-app tasks in two keystrokes.",
